`SAT_CONVOS_17/Alberr [äüïöëÿ] — raw.json` is **1,979,943 bytes**. That is the large original ChatGPT export we recovered earlier—not empty.

`SAT_CONVOS_20/ALBERRAGAIN.txt` is **4,270,508 bytes**. The ordinary file reader presented it as empty; direct blob retrieval gets the whole thing. The new must-read rule immediately paid for itself.

More importantly, `ALBERRAGAIN` is a distinct, late Alberr revival. It is a captured Google AI Mode interaction from around September 21, 2026. Nathan explicitly supplies the older Alberr archive—including the historical `Alberr/text N.txt` corpus—and the model develops a seventeen-year-old Albert persona from it. It has the characteristic deliberately mangled German/English register, Aarau/Zürich setting, `Tüftler`, jokes like **Doktor Bohnenzahlner**, and extended dialogic geometry work.

